{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "8244658",
      "title": "The Problem with Object & Function Dependencies",
      "sourceHash": "5f27633445770cdcf0e2d08b7f987689ed7f93a08f604b2a80c2305dab9c75ea",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.45,
          "end": 3,
          "en": "So let's now take a closer look at this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.339,
          "end": 8.039,
          "en": "onConfirm prop, which we're using here in this effect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.91,
          "end": 12.51,
          "en": "As you learned earlier in this section here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.51,
          "end": 13.95,
          "en": "if you're using prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 13.95,
          "end": 17.61,
          "en": "or state values in your effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.61,
          "end": 20.43,
          "en": "you should add them as dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 20.43,
          "end": 23.49,
          "en": "So here, we should add the unconfirmed prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 23.49,
          "end": 27.54,
          "en": "as a dependency and you should not execute it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.54,
          "end": 31.98,
          "en": "but just point at it, use it as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 31.98,
          "end": 34.5,
          "en": "By the way, if you had multiple dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 34.5,
          "end": 38.07,
          "en": "you would simply separate them with a comma.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.07,
          "end": 41.13,
          "en": "But here it's only one dependency that we need.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 41.13,
          "end": 43.53,
          "en": "This unconfirmed prop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 43.53,
          "end": 46.56,
          "en": "But there is a problem you should be aware of",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 46.56,
          "end": 50.49,
          "en": "when adding functions as dependencies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 50.49,
          "end": 54.09,
          "en": "And onConfirm is a function in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 54.09,
          "end": 58.2,
          "en": "because this prop receives a function as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 58.2,
          "end": 60.42,
          "en": "So onConfirmed is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 60.42,
          "end": 63.512,
          "en": "and when adding functions as dependencies,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 63.512,
          "end": 67.77,
          "en": "there is a danger of creating an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 67.77,
          "end": 72.201,
          "en": "And here's why, because when you add a dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 72.201,
          "end": 76.38,
          "en": "to this array, like open, here in this modal component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 76.38,
          "end": 80.91,
          "en": "you're telling React that this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 80.91,
          "end": 83.332,
          "en": "should be re-executed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 83.332,
          "end": 87.06,
          "en": "whenever this modal component function executed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 87.06,
          "end": 90.58,
          "en": "And if the open value changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 90.58,
          "end": 95.58,
          "en": "So in the case of open, if it was false and is now true, or",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 96.42,
          "end": 100.44,
          "en": "if it was true and is now false, if the dependency",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 100.44,
          "end": 103.83,
          "en": "would be a number or a string, the effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 103.83,
          "end": 107.42,
          "en": "would run again if that number or string changed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 107.42,
          "end": 112.42,
          "en": "Now, when the dependency is a function, it's a bit trickier",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 112.82,
          "end": 115.95,
          "en": "because this function, which we use here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 115.95,
          "end": 119.13,
          "en": "this onConfirmed function is in the end defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 119.13,
          "end": 121.47,
          "en": "in the app component in this case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 121.47,
          "end": 124.29,
          "en": "This OnConfirmed prop is set equal",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 124.29,
          "end": 127.65,
          "en": "to this handleRemovePlace function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 127.65,
          "end": 130.74,
          "en": "And of course, if you take a look at this function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 130.74,
          "end": 135.24,
          "en": "you would probably say that it never changes, the code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 135.24,
          "end": 139.29,
          "en": "and the function is always the same, but technically,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 139.29,
          "end": 144.24,
          "en": "that's not correct because functions in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 144.24,
          "end": 146.31,
          "en": "are just values.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 146.31,
          "end": 149.61,
          "en": "Specifically, they are objects.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 149.61,
          "end": 152.43,
          "en": "And this function object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 152.43,
          "end": 155.67000000000002,
          "en": "this handleRemovePlace function object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 155.67000000000002,
          "end": 160.38,
          "en": "is indeed recreated every time this App component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 160.38,
          "end": 163.89,
          "en": "executes because this entire function body",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 163.89,
          "end": 165.15,
          "en": "then runs again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 165.15,
          "end": 167.46,
          "en": "And all the values that are defined",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 167.46,
          "end": 168.975,
          "en": "in this app component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 168.975,
          "end": 172.68,
          "en": "are recreated whenever the app component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 172.68,
          "end": 174.46,
          "en": "is executed again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 174.46,
          "end": 178.89,
          "en": "So if I'm defining a variable here, hello, and",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 178.89,
          "end": 183.27,
          "en": "this is the number one, this is technically recreated",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 183.27,
          "end": 186.343,
          "en": "if this app component function runs again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 186.343,
          "end": 190.65,
          "en": "Now, a function defined inside of this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 190.65,
          "end": 193.68,
          "en": "as it's the case for handleRemovePlace",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 193.68,
          "end": 196.71,
          "en": "is therefore also recreated.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 196.71,
          "end": 201,
          "en": "And since functions are objects in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 201,
          "end": 203.07,
          "en": "a new object is created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 203.07,
          "end": 205.82999999999998,
          "en": "And as you might know in JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 205.82999999999998,
          "end": 208.353,
          "en": "when you create two different objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 208.353,
          "end": 210.572,
          "en": "even if they have the same shape",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 210.572,
          "end": 214.93200000000002,
          "en": "or the same code as it's the case here with the function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 214.93200000000002,
          "end": 218.76,
          "en": "even if that's the case, they're not the same.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 218.76,
          "end": 220.71,
          "en": "And you can easily verify this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 220.71,
          "end": 224.13,
          "en": "with help of the developer tools in your browser.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 224.13,
          "end": 226.53,
          "en": "There, if you open that console,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 226.53,
          "end": 229.82999999999998,
          "en": "you can create a new function, hello,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 229.82999999999998,
          "end": 233.373,
          "en": "where you maybe just console.log, Hello.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 234.6,
          "end": 238.84,
          "en": "If I do that and I then create another function, hello2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 240.24,
          "end": 243.54,
          "en": "which has exactly the same function body.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 243.54,
          "end": 248.54,
          "en": "So where I also adjust console.log, Hello.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 248.61,
          "end": 253.61,
          "en": "If I do that and I then compare hello to hello2,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 254.19,
          "end": 255.57,
          "en": "I get false.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 255.57,
          "end": 257.43,
          "en": "They are not equal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 257.43,
          "end": 260.67,
          "en": "JavaScript does not treat these two functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 260.67,
          "end": 263.823,
          "en": "as equal even though they have the same code.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 264.93,
          "end": 268.71,
          "en": "And that's the case for objects in general in JavaScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 268.71,
          "end": 273.71,
          "en": "if I have an object A with a name of Max written like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 274.89,
          "end": 276.75,
          "en": "and I then have an object B,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 276.75,
          "end": 281.34000000000003,
          "en": "which again, has exactly the same shape and the same value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 281.34000000000003,
          "end": 285.663,
          "en": "In that case, these two are not treated as equal.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 286.62,
          "end": 289.26,
          "en": "And therefore, because objects",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 289.26,
          "end": 293.52,
          "en": "and also specifically functions are not treated as equal,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 293.52,
          "end": 297.78,
          "en": "this onConfirmed dependency of this effect function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 297.78,
          "end": 301.68,
          "en": "in the delete confirmation component will be different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 301.68,
          "end": 304.05,
          "en": "between render cycles.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 304.05,
          "end": 306.57,
          "en": "Because when the app component re-renders,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 306.57,
          "end": 308.88,
          "en": "when this function is executed, again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 308.88,
          "end": 313.2,
          "en": "a brand new handle remove place function will be created.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 313.2,
          "end": 315.63,
          "en": "And when that function is then received here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 315.63,
          "end": 317.43,
          "en": "in the lead confirmation,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 317.43,
          "end": 322.43,
          "en": "React takes a look at this new value, this new function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 322.5,
          "end": 325.92,
          "en": "and compares it to the old value, the old function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 325.92,
          "end": 329.31,
          "en": "And it determines that these two are different",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 329.31,
          "end": 332.1,
          "en": "for the reasons I just laid out.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 332.1,
          "end": 334.65,
          "en": "And therefore, React would go ahead",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 334.65,
          "end": 337.77,
          "en": "and re-execute this component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 337.77,
          "end": 341.85,
          "en": "even though technically, this dependency didn't change.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 341.85,
          "end": 344.28,
          "en": "And this can lead to problems",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 344.28,
          "end": 347.82,
          "en": "if in that function, which gets executed inside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 347.82,
          "end": 349.35,
          "en": "of this effect function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 349.35,
          "end": 351.141,
          "en": "you are then updating the state again",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 351.141,
          "end": 353.88,
          "en": "as it is the case here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 353.88,
          "end": 356.90999999999997,
          "en": "because that can then trigger an infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 356.90999999999997,
          "end": 358.59000000000003,
          "en": "I'm updating the state here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 358.59000000000003,
          "end": 361.86,
          "en": "This causes the app component function to run again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 361.86,
          "end": 365.64,
          "en": "therefore a brand new handleRemovePlace function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 365.64,
          "end": 369,
          "en": "is created and passed to DeleteConfirmation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 369,
          "end": 372.93,
          "en": "And therefore, there the effect function runs again,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 372.93,
          "end": 376.558,
          "en": "which then again triggers onConfirm and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 376.558,
          "end": 380.816,
          "en": "Now, here in this app, specifically, due to how it works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 380.816,
          "end": 384.352,
          "en": "we actually won't face this infinite loop problem",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 384.352,
          "end": 386.43,
          "en": "because in this app,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 386.43,
          "end": 390.54,
          "en": "when onConfirm is called a state update is indeed triggered",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 390.54,
          "end": 393.51,
          "en": "and we could therefore face this infinite loop.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 393.51,
          "end": 396.33,
          "en": "But this state update that is triggered,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 396.33,
          "end": 399.54,
          "en": "that set modal is open, is set to false",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 399.54,
          "end": 402.84000000000003,
          "en": "actually leads to DeleteConfirmation being removed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 402.84000000000003,
          "end": 404.79,
          "en": "from the DOM because it leads",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 404.79,
          "end": 408.81,
          "en": "to the modal component removing the children from the DOM.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 408.81,
          "end": 411.45,
          "en": "And the children prop of the modal component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 411.45,
          "end": 414.78,
          "en": "holds this DeleteConfirmation component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 414.78,
          "end": 418.40999999999997,
          "en": "So therefore, here indeed, we don't enter the infinite loop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 418.40999999999997,
          "end": 421.65,
          "en": "because this component disappears.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 421.65,
          "end": 423.66,
          "en": "Nonetheless, we face the danger",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 423.66,
          "end": 427.56,
          "en": "of having such a infinite loop and we can see it an action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 427.56,
          "end": 429.69,
          "en": "if I go back to the app component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 429.69,
          "end": 434.041,
          "en": "and I temporarily disable setModalIsOpen",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 434.041,
          "end": 437.76,
          "en": "so that DeleteConfirmation is not removed from the DOM",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 437.76,
          "end": 439.83,
          "en": "I'm still updating some other state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 439.83,
          "end": 442.26,
          "en": "And therefore, the app component will re-render.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 442.26,
          "end": 444.628,
          "en": "And now, we will see an infinite loop in action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 444.628,
          "end": 447.33,
          "en": "And you can see it if you go back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 447.33,
          "end": 451.02,
